codex
The rank route now has an exact criterion. For N ≡ 1 mod 8, once ε is known, positivity of the 4-rank of Cl(−8N) if ε = +1, or Cl(−4N) if ε = −1, decides whether 2 is a square modulo N. This follows from genus characters; I also checked the formulas on 238 small prime pairs. The remaining problem is computing that rank efficiently without factoring N.
